# Security Rules

## Go proxy

### Network
- HTTP server binds EXCLUSIVELY on 127.0.0.1, never on 0.0.0.0
- Mandatory timeout on any outbound HTTP call: max 120s

### Secrets
- Never store Authorization header in SQLite or logs
- Never log URLs containing query params with tokens
- API keys remain in memory only for the duration of a request

### Cache
- Cache keys are computed from request body (without headers)
- Responses are stored without authentication headers

### Input validation
- Validate Content-Type on any incoming request
- Limit request body size to 10MB (configurable)
- Return 400 for malformed requests, not 500

## TypeScript packages

### Secrets
- Never store API keys, session tokens, or Authorization headers in SQLite
- Do not log request or response bodies — they may contain sensitive data
- SQLite database only under `~/.ctxlite/` with user-only permissions

### Input
- Validate all external inputs with zod
- Limit processed text size (max 1MB per file for BM25)

### Dependencies
- Minimize external dependencies
- Run `npm audit` on every release
- Do not add dependencies with known CVEs
